# The share of this machine the browsers may use, so the production services keep running when a page eats the CPU. There is NO hard CPU quota on purpose: round nine
# (design doc §3.3) suggests (weakly) that a quota makes the picture stutter in bursts; a low weight lets the other services win when the machine is busy and lets the
# browser use what it needs when it is not. Memory is still limited. The browser containers join it
# with  docker run --cgroup-parent=noureon-browser.slice  (P1). Numbers are a start: measure, then change them.
[Unit]
Description=Noureon browser containers (limited share of the machine)

[Slice]
CPUWeight=20
MemoryHigh=3500M
MemoryMax=4G
MemorySwapMax=0
TasksMax=2048
